cf-mail2telegram CF Worker notes
================================

Inbound mail → AI OTP (Gemini → CUSTOM free → local regex) → Telegram (Preview + Mailbox)


1) KV (required)
----------------

Bind a KV namespace to this Worker:

  Worker → Bindings → KV Namespace
  Variable name must be: DB


2) Variables
------------

Secrets (recommended):

  TELEGRAM_BOT              token,chat_id
  GEMINI_OFFICIAL_API_KEY   Google AI Studio key (AIza…)
  CUSTOM_API_KEY            OpenRouter (or other OpenAI-compatible) key
  WEB_USER                  username,password  (optional; web login for /email + /init)


Vars:

  UI_LANG            en (default) | zh | tw

  AI_PROVIDER        GEMINI_OFFICIAL,CUSTOM   (order = fallback order)

  GEMINI_OFFICIAL_API_MODEL
                     gemini-2.5-flash,gemini-2.5-flash-lite,gemini-2.0-flash

  CUSTOM_API_BASE    https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
  CUSTOM_API_MODEL   google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free,poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free

  FORWARD_MAIL      Single backup:
                     email[,GmailFolder][,noforwarded|forwarded]
                     e.g. you+bak@gmail.com,Backup,noforwarded
                     Default policy: noforwarded
                     Hard rule: never backup when From / To-related
                     headers match the backup address (Gmail +tag)

  DEBUG              true → show LLM error on local OTP fallback


No DOMAIN variable.
Public host is saved when you open /init (KV key PUBLIC_HOST).

Preview:
  Default Mini App; /previewmode switches to Web (warns; copy depends on WEB_USER).
  Mail cache: hard max 100 bodies.
  Without WEB_USER: /email/<id>?t=<token>, hard 1d expiry + countdown.
  With WEB_USER: /email/<id> needs login page; /init needs login; status page stays public.


Mailbox:
  backed up     → FORWARD_MAIL
  not backed up → original header To webmail (if Gmail/Outlook)


Required:  TELEGRAM_BOT, DB (KV binding name must be DB)
Recommended: AI_PROVIDER + keys, FORWARD_MAIL, WEB_USER, UI_LANG

Optional defaults (usually leave alone):
  TIMEZONE           Asia/Shanghai   (mail Time line)
  GMAIL_U            0               (Mailbox → Gmail /mail/u/N/ slot; not multi-inbox)


3) Deploy
---------

keep_vars=true — dashboard plain Vars survive deploy.

After deploy open the Worker public URL (status page), then click the center status text to run /init
(orb → GitHub; blank area does nothing; 1.5s debounce). Or open .../init directly.

  Mode A (workers.dev — two levels before workers.dev):
    https://mail2telegram.your-subdomain.workers.dev

  Mode B (your own domain routed to this Worker):
    https://mail.example.com

JSON/toast should show host. Re-run /init after changing UI_LANG or switching primary host.


4) Checklist
------------

  [ ] KV binding name DB
  [ ] TELEGRAM_BOT
  [ ] WEB_USER optional (username,password)
  [ ] UI_LANG if you want zh or tw
  [ ] AI_PROVIDER + GEMINI_OFFICIAL_API_KEY / CUSTOM_API_KEY for AI OTP
  [ ] FORWARD_MAIL verified in Email Routing destinations
  [ ] BotFather Mini App URL + Privacy Policy URL
  [ ] Email Routing → this Worker
  [ ] Visited /init
  [ ] Remove obsolete GEMINI_API / GEMINI_MODEL / MAILS_TTL / INIT_SECRET vars if present
